THOUGHT: The PASS_NULLABLE error is from calling `c.minHeight.get(c.actor)` when `c.actor` is @Nullable. The simplest safe fix is to avoid calling `get` when `actor` is null and instead use a neutral value (0) for min sizes, since a null actor is not laid out (note the later `if (c.actor != null) c.actor.setBounds(...)`). I’ll update the layout code to compute a local `minHeight` (and similarly `minWidth`, `maxWidth`, `maxHeight` for consistency) that uses 0 when `c.actor` is null, then rerun the compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && \
apply_edits() { sed -i "$1" gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Table.java; } && \
apply_edits '1195,1207s/fillX = c.fillX, fillY = c.fillY;/fillX = c.fillX, fillY = c.fillY;
      float minWidth = c.actor == null ? 0 : c.minWidth.get(c.actor);
      float maxWidth = c.actor == null ? 0 : c.maxWidth.get(c.actor);
      float minHeight = c.actor == null ? 0 : c.minHeight.get(c.actor);
      float maxHeight = c.actor == null ? 0 : c.maxHeight.get(c.actor);/' && \
apply_edits '1196,1199s/c.actorWidth = Math.max(spannedCellWidth * fillX, c.minWidth.get(c.actor));/c.actorWidth = Math.max(spannedCellWidth * fillX, minWidth);/' && \
apply_edits '1198,1199s/float maxWidth = c.maxWidth.get(c.actor);
        if (maxWidth > 0) c.actorWidth = Math.min(c.actorWidth, maxWidth);/if (maxWidth > 0) c.actorWidth = Math.min(c.actorWidth, maxWidth);/' && \
apply_edits '1202,1207s/Math.max(
                rowHeight[c.row] * fillY - c.computedPadTop - c.computedPadBottom,
                c.minHeight.get(c.actor));
        float maxHeight = c.maxHeight.get(c.actor);
        if (maxHeight > 0) c.actorHeight = Math.min(c.actorHeight, maxHeight);/Math.max(
                rowHeight[c.row] * fillY - c.computedPadTop - c.computedPadBottom,
                minHeight);
        if (maxHeight > 0) c.actorHeight = Math.min(c.actorHeight, maxHeight);/' && \
./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && \
grep -E "NullAway|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log

